:: Underground Colosseum Wrong Exit
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>>
<<pass 2>>
A bout ends while you are standing near the top of the seating. The losing fighter stays on the sand after the referee finishes the count.
<br><br>
Two attendants enter the pit and help <<him>> to <<his>> feet. <<He>> is awake, but <<his>> legs are unsteady, so they support <<him>> between them.
They lead <<him>> towards the service corridor. That way normally leads to the medical room.
<br><br>
Before they reach it, a security worker steps in front of the corridor and blocks the way. The attendants stop, turn around, and take the injured fighter behind the betting booths instead.
They bring <<him>> to a plain grey door. One attendant unlocks it, then both of them take <<him>> inside.
<br><br>
You were shown the medical room when you registered. It is nowhere near that door.
<br><br>
Why would they take an injured fighter somewhere else?
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask the receptionist about it|Underground Colosseum Wrong Exit Ask]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say nothing|Underground Colosseum]]>><<colosseumStoryAdvance 1>><<colosseumHeat 2>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Wrong Exit Ask
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<colosseumHost>>
You wait until the receptionist finishes with another fighter, then point towards the grey door behind the betting booths.
<br><br>
"What's through there?" you ask.
<br><br>
"Storage," <<he>> says without looking up. "Beer, cleaning supplies, things like that."
<br><br>
"I just saw two attendants take an injured fighter through it. The medical room is the other way," you press.
<br><br>
The receptionist stops writing and puts the cap on <<his>> pen. <<He>> looks at you before answering.
"Then you already know there is more back there than storage."
<br><br>
You ask what the attendants were doing.
<br><br>
"I can't tell. Staff are told to call that door storage. That's the answer we're expected to give." <<He>> glances towards the betting booths, then looks back at you.
"You're doing well here. You get regular fights, people recognise you, and the house pays you. If you keep asking about that door, someone above me may start asking why you're so interested."
<<colosseumStoryAdvance 1>><<colosseumHeat 3 "The receptionist avoided explaining why injured fighters are taken through the grey door.">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Pit]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Familiar Contestant
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>>
<<pass 2>>
A fighter waits beside the changing cages in a loose robe. <<His>> face looks familiar. After another look, you realise you have seen <<him>> working in town before. <<He>> has served you as a customer.
<br><br>
<<He>> notices that you recognise <<him>>. <<He>> looks away and lowers <<his>> voice.
"Please don't tell anyone here where I work."

<<link [[Ask why <<he>> is here|Underground Colosseum Familiar Answer]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Leave <<him>> alone|Underground Colosseum Pit]]>><<colosseumStoryAdvance 2>><<colosseumHeat 1>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Familiar Answer
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<person1>>
<<pass 5>>
You ask why <<he>> started fighting here. At first <<he>> only says that <<he>> needed money. You wait instead of changing the subject, and after checking that nobody nearby is listening, <<he>> explains the rest.
<br><br>
"I owed someone money. One purse here would have covered the whole amount, so I signed up for one fight." <<He>> rubs one thumb over the strap of <<his>> robe.
<br><br>
"I lost the first fight, but the house still paid me appearance money. I thought that meant I had not wasted the trip. Then I came back to make up the rest. After that there was another fight, then another."
<br><br>
You ask how many bouts <<he>> has fought now.
<br><br>
"Eleven." <<He>> looks towards the cages before continuing.
"The payment is what keeps you coming back. Even when you lose, you leave with some money, so it is easy to tell yourself the next fight will fix the problem."
<br><br>
You look at <<him>>. "And you still owe money?"
<br><br>
"More than before," <<he>> says.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Familiar Answer 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Familiar Answer 2
<<effects>>
You ask how that happened.
<br><br>
"They charge for staying here, for food, and for treatment when you get hurt," <<he>> explains. "I kept thinking the next fight would earn enough to cover everything, but the fees kept adding up."
<br><br>
Before you can ask more, an attendant calls <<his>> arena name from the pit. <<He>> turns towards the sound. "That's me."
<br><br>
<<He>> stands and heads towards the ramp for <<his>> next fight. <<colosseumStoryAdvance 2>><<colosseumHeat 4 "A fighter came for one purse, but repeated fights and house fees left <<him>> owing more than before.">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Pit]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Grey Door
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>>
<<pass 2>>
You enter the fighters' bar and order a drink. When the bartender comes over, you ask about the grey door behind the betting booths.
<br><br>
<<He>> stops cleaning a glass. "What about it?"
<br><br>
You say you have seen injured fighters taken through it, even though the receptionist claims it only leads to storage.
<br><br>
"It does lead to storage," <<he>> says. "Beer, food, cleaning supplies. But there are stairs at the back that go down another level."
<br><br>
You ask what is downstairs.
<br><br>
"I don't know. Staff don't talk about it." <<He>> looks towards the bar entrance, then continues.
"Someone comes here once a week with a list of names. They speak to the staff, then take the list through that door."
<br><br>
You ask whose names are on it.
<br><br>
"Fighters. I recognise some of them. Most owe the Colosseum money." <<He>> puts the glass down.
"That's all I know. Don't tell anyone I said this. I need this job."
<<colosseumStoryAdvance 3>><<colosseumHeat 3 "A person with a folder checks the names of fighters who owe money, then goes through the grey door.">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Pit]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Downstairs
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>>
<<pass 5>>
You wait near the betting booths until two workers arrive with a delivery. They carry several crates through the grey door, leaving it open while they return for the rest.
<br><br>
You pick up one of the crates and follow them inside.
<br><br>
The first room is used for storage. Beer, cleaning supplies and folded chairs are stacked around the walls. A staircase at the back leads farther down.
<br><br>
You leave the crate with the others. Once the workers go back upstairs, you take the stairs down.
<br><br>
A narrow corridor runs beneath the Colosseum. Small rooms line both sides, each with a window in the door so staff can look inside.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Downstairs 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Downstairs 2
<<effects>>
A fighter sits on the edge of a stained mattress, wrapping a strip of cloth around <<his>> swollen hand. <<He>> tries to bend <<his>> fingers, but they barely move.
An untouched bowl of cold food is on the floor by <<his>> feet.
<br><br>
Beside the door is a small list of charges for the room, meals, bandages, and other expenses. At the bottom, someone has added a fine for missing a scheduled fight.
<br><br>
You look at the current fight list. The injured fighter is still expected to compete.
<br><br>
"If I don't fight, they charge me again... or worse," <<he>> says quietly. <<He>> looks towards the stairs. "Please go. I don't want them asking why you're talking to me."
<br><br>
Footsteps come down the stairs. You pick up an empty crate and walk back towards the delivery workers before the attendant reaches the corridor.
<<colosseumStoryAdvance 4>><<colosseumHeat 4 "Injured fighters are kept downstairs while room charges and missed-fight fines make their debts grow.">>
<br><br>
<<link [[Return to the pit|Underground Colosseum Pit]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum VIP Invitation
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<colosseumHost>>
<<pass 2>>
Before you reach the match board, the receptionist leaves the fighters' desk and approaches you.
"The people in the private gallery want to meet you upstairs."
<br><br>
You glance towards the dark glass above the seating.
<br><br>
<<He>> checks that nobody is waiting behind you, then lowers <<his>> voice. "I can tell them you're ill. Gets you out of the room, but they'll take it out of your purse. At least a quarter of your next payout."
<<He>> taps your name on the booking sheet. "Their money. Their petty fucking rules. Your call."
<br><br>
<<link [[Go up|Underground Colosseum VIP Gallery]]>><<colosseumStoryAdvance 5>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Ask <<him>> to make an excuse|Underground Colosseum VIP Decline]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum VIP Decline
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<colosseumHost>>
"Tell them I'm unwell."
<br><br>
The receptionist puts the booking sheet face down and goes upstairs without you.
<br><br>
When <<he>> returns, <<he>> takes a red pencil from the till and marks your next booking.
<br><br>
"They send their sympathy." <<He>> turns the sheet so you can see the deduction. "At least a quarter off your next purse. That's what sympathy costs upstairs."
<br><br>
<<set $xchange.colosseum.vipPenalty to Math.min($xchange.colosseum.vipPenalty ?? 1, 0.75)>><<colosseumHeat 2>>
<br><br>
