:: Underground Colosseum VIP Gallery
<<if $xchange.colosseum.story gte 6>>
	<<include "Underground Colosseum Gallery Desk">>
<<else>>
	<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>>
	<<pass 5>>
	An attendant unlocks the stairs to the private gallery and leads you up.
	<br><br>
	The room overlooks the arena through thick glass. Eight people are waiting inside. Some have drinks beside them, while two hide their faces behind decorative masks.
	<br><br>
	One <<person>> stands apart from the others with a folder under <<his>> arm. The bartender mentioned someone who keeps records connected to the grey door. You suspect this is <<him>>.
	<br><br>
	At first, the group asks about your fights: how long you have competed, how often you fight, and how much the house normally pays you. Two of them comment that they have paid much more for private matches.
	<br><br>
	Then the questions become personal.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum VIP Gallery 2]]>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>

:: Underground Colosseum VIP Gallery 2
<<effects>>
They ask where you live, whether you have family nearby, and whether anyone relies on the money you earn. One asks if you would fight privately for them instead of appearing on the normal match board.
<br><br>
Another asks about your arena name. When you explain that the crowd gave it to you, they become more interested in how many spectators recognise you.
<br><br>
The <<person>> with the folder finally opens it. "Do you owe money to the house?"
<br><br>
<<if $xchange.colosseum.debt gt 0>>
	Before you answer, <<he>> reads out <span class="gold"><<printmoney $xchange.colosseum.debt>></span>. "Don't bullshit me. We keep the book."
<<else>>
	"Nothing?" <<He>> checks the account column. "For now." The pen scratches beside your name.
<</if>>
<br><br>
You understand what they are checking now. They want to know how useful you are, how much money might persuade you, and whether debt or someone close to you could be used to pressure you.
<<if $xchange.colosseum.story lt 5>><<colosseumStoryAdvance 5>><</if>>
<<colosseumHeat 3>><<stress 6>><<ggstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Terraces]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Championship
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "colosseum">><<effects>><<generate1>><<person1>>
<<pass 3>>
After reaching the highest rank, an attendant takes you back to the private gallery.
The person with the folder is waiting at the table. Several other gallery members stay nearby to listen.
<br><br>
"Your name fills seats," <<he>> says, tapping a column of takings. "That makes you useful. Sign as house champion and we stop wasting you on the cheap cards."
<br><br>
You ask what that means.
<br><br>
"More money for every fight. We advertise your name, give you the biggest matches, and keep you at the centre of the Colosseum." <<He>> opens the folder.
"In return, we choose who you fight. Sometimes we buy the result before the bell. If we tell you to win, you win. If we tell you to lose, you make sure you lose."
<br><br>
You ask what happens if you refuse.
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Underground Colosseum Championship 2]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Underground Colosseum Championship 2
<<effects>>
"Then fuck off out of this office." <<He>> closes the folder. "There's a queue of desperate bastards downstairs who'd sign with a broken hand."
<br><br>
You think about the fighters downstairs who are still trying to pay off their debts. Becoming champion would give you better pay and keep you away from that situation, but the gallery would control your matches.
<br><br>
<<link [[Take the deal|Underground Colosseum Champion Embrace]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Take the deal and copy the records|Underground Colosseum Champion Exploit]]>><<endevent>><</link>><<skill_difficulty `currentSkillValue("skulduggery")` "Skulduggery" 0 1000>>
